      "category": "via-citation",
      "published": "",
      "collected": "2026-06-03",
      "abstract": "Code authorship attribution (CAA) supports software forensics, plagiarism detection, and intellectual property protection. However, existing supervised CAA approaches suffer from scarce training data and closed-world assumptions: they require sufficient labeled code from fixed candidate-author sets, making training difficult in low-data cases and predictions unreliable for open-world test pairs with unseen samples, or heterogeneous code pairs. Large language models remove task-specific training, but direct prompting depends on costly expert-designed prompts, can hallucinate over complex heterogeneous code pairs, and rarely yields auditable evidence traces. We propose MACAA, a belief-revision-based multi-agent framework for training-free code authorship verification. MACAA comprises a Coordinator and four Expert Agents analyzing layout, lexical, syntactic, and programming-pattern evidence. The Coordinator gathers expert signals for expansion, discounts unreliable evidence through contraction, and resolves conflicts through revision to preserve belief consistency, replacing direct LLM judgment with auditable hypothesis refinement. MACAA achieves 89.15\\% F1 on same-language benchmarks and 80.00\\% on mixed cross-language pairs, outperforming the baselines overall in both same-language and cross-language evaluations.",
      "abstract_zh": "代码作者身份验证（CAA）可支持软件取证、抄袭检测与知识产权保护。现有监督CAA方法存在训练数据稀缺、闭世界假设问题，需固定候选集足量标注代码，低数据场景训练难，开世界未知样本、异构代码对预测不可靠。大语言模型无需任务训练，但直接提示依赖昂贵专家prompt，对复杂异构对易幻觉，缺少可追溯证据。本文提出基于信念修正的无训练多智能体框架MACAA，整合多专家证据修正信念，在基准上F1分别达89.15%和80.00%，性能优于基线。",
